.TH "CRUFT" "1" "September 2026" "cruft" "cruft User Manual"
.SH NAME
.PP
cruft \- Calculinux reduced footprint framebuffer terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.B cruft
.RB [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B cruft
is a Linux framebuffer terminal emulator derived from yaft, tuned for
low memory on Calculinux devices.
.PP
The alternate screen buffer (DECALT) is implemented, so full-screen
programs (vim, htop, less) run on their own buffer and leave the main
screen intact when they exit.
.PP
When a status font is installed, cruft draws a status bar in the margin
strip above the cell grid: the window title set by the foreground
program on the left, the clock in the centre, and a wifi signal stair
and battery indicator on the right. The title is the standard terminal
window title (escape sequence OSC 0/2, the same channel xterm-style
terminal emulators show in their title bars), so shells, editors and
other programs announce the current file or command; an empty title
clears it. Non-ASCII characters are dropped (the 4x8 status font has
no such coverage), and the title is trimmed so it never overlaps the
centred clock. A segment whose data source is absent (bare hardware,
VM) is hidden; a missing or unsuitable status font disables the bar
entirely and the grid reclaims the full screen.
.SH CUSTOMIZATION
.PP
Rewrite conf.h before make.
The default status bar segment selection (used when
.B CRUFT_SB
is unset) is the
.B sb_default_segments
conf.h variable (default "all").
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B FRAMEBUFFER
Specify framebuffer device (default /dev/fb0).
.TP
.B CRUFT_FONT
Path to a CRUFTFN1 font blob (default /usr/share/cruft/console.cruftfont).
.TP
.B CRUFT
If this variable includes "wall", cruft enables wallpaper mode and a
framebuffer shadow buffer. See cruft_wall.
.TP
.B CRUFT_SB
Status bar segments: a comma-separated list of
.B time ,
.B wifi ,
.B battery
and
.BR title ,
or
.B all
(the default) to show every segment whose source is present,
.B none
(or
.BR 0 )
to disable the bar. Unknown names are ignored with a warning.
.TP
.B CRUFT_SB_12H
Set to 1 for a 12-hour clock (\fIH:MMam/pm\fP); the default is
24-hour.
.TP
.B CRUFT_SB_FONT
Path to the 4x8 CRUFTFN1 status font
(default /usr/share/cruft/status.cruftfont, installed by the
miniwi-console package).
